## 4. Model Architecture

Three parallel, purpose-fit components, fused into one verdict per test instance:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Raw telemetry CSVs<br/>cell: V, I, T @1Hz &nbsp; bus: V, I×3 @100Hz] --> B{real_battery_data_used?}

    B -- True --> C[Cell-level pipeline]
    B -- False --> H[Bus-level pipeline]

    subgraph C[Cell-level: battery health]
        direction TB
        C1[Coulomb counting<br/>SOC via ∫I dt] --> C2[Reference curve V_ref(SOC)<br/>built once from healthy cell]
        C2 --> C3[1RC Equivalent-Circuit Model<br/>V = V_ref(SOC) − I·R0 − V_RC]
        C3 --> C4[Extended Kalman Filter<br/>state = SOC, V_RC]
        C4 --> C5[Residual / innovation<br/>y = V_meas − V_pred]
        C5 --> C6[Threshold rule<br/>resid_max, max dT/dt]
        C1 --> C7[Differential Capacity Analysis<br/>dQ/dV vs V, Savitzky-Golay smoothed]
        C7 --> C8[Peak-voltage shift vs healthy]
        C6 --> F[Cell verdict]
        C8 --> F
    end

    subgraph H[Bus-level: distribution health]
        direction TB
        H1[Healthy-run baseline<br/>mean, std of V_bus & branch I] --> H2[Percentile features<br/>1st pct V, 99th pct I]
        H2 --> H3[Z-score threshold rule<br/>undervoltage / overcurrent]
    end

    F --> Z[Fused system-health verdict<br/>H / UH per instance]
    H3 --> Z
    Z --> R[Comparison vs manifest ground truth<br/>+ accuracy report]
```

### 4.1 Cell-level: Equivalent-Circuit Model (ECM)

1st-order Thevenin/RC model:

```
V(t) = V_ref(SOC(t)) − (I(t) − I_ref)·R0 − V_RC(t)
dV_RC/dt = −V_RC / (R1·C1) + I(t) / C1
```

- `V_ref(SOC)`: empirical curve built by mapping the healthy reference discharge onto SOC (via coulomb
  counting) and smoothing with Savitzky–Golay. Acts as the OCV-analog in this reduced model.
- `R0` (ohmic resistance), `R1`, `C1` (single RC branch: polarization resistance/capacitance) — fixed to
  representative small-format Li-ion literature values (see §6) because this dataset can't identify them
  independently (see §2 limitation).

### 4.2 Cell-level: Extended Kalman Filter (EKF)

- **State vector:** `x = [SOC (%), V_RC (V)]`
- **Process model:** SOC updated by coulomb counting (`ΔSOC = -100·I·Δt / (3600·Qmax)`); `V_RC` updated by
  the RC discharge/charge equation above.
- **Measurement model:** `h(x) = V_ref(SOC) − (I − I_ref)·R0 − V_RC`, linearized each step via a numeric
  Jacobian of `V_ref` w.r.t. SOC (central difference, `ε = 1e-3`).
- **Output per sample:** updated state estimate `[SOC, V_RC]` and the innovation/residual
  `y = V_measured − h(x_predicted)` — this residual is the primary real-time anomaly signal.

### 4.3 Cell-level: Differential Capacity Analysis (dQ/dV, ICA)

- Compute cumulative capacity `Q(t)` (mAh) via coulomb counting.
- Resample `Q` onto a uniform voltage grid (300 points), smooth with Savitzky–Golay, then
  `dQ/dV = np.gradient(Q_smooth, V_grid)`.
- Compare the voltage location of the peak `dQ/dV` against the healthy reference — a shift indicates
  electrode/impedance changes associated with degradation.

### 4.4 Bus-level: rule-based statistical detector

- Baseline `mean, std` of bus voltage and each branch current computed from the healthy runs only.
- Per-instance features: 1st-percentile bus voltage (z-scored) and max of the 99th-percentile branch
  currents (z-scored) — percentiles chosen over raw min/max because raw extreme values are noisy over
  180,000-sample runs.
- Simple threshold rule flags `UH (undervoltage)` / `UH (overcurrent)` / `H`.

### 4.5 Fusion layer

- Cell-origin instances: `UH` if **either** the EKF residual rule fires **or** the dQ/dV peak shift exceeds
  its threshold (OR-fusion — either signal is sufficient to flag).
- Bus-origin instances: `UH` if the bus rule fires.
- Final per-instance verdict is compared against `manifest.label` to compute accuracy.

