## 6. Training Process

This pipeline is **not a trained ML model** in the gradient-descent sense — it's a physics-based estimator
(EKF) plus signal-processing diagnostics (dQ/dV) plus calibrated statistical thresholds. "Training" here
means **parameter identification and threshold calibration**, done once from the healthy reference data:

| Component | "Training" step | Value used | Calibration data |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Qmax_healthy` | total Ah delivered by healthy cell | ≈ 0.913 Ah | `cell/normal_000.csv` |
| `V_ref(SOC)` | Savitzky–Golay smoothing (window=51, polyorder=3) of healthy V vs. coulomb-counted SOC | curve (300+ pts) | `cell/normal_000.csv` |
| `R0` | fixed (literature-typical, not identifiable from this dataset — see §2) | 0.05 Ω | — |
| `R1, C1` | fixed (literature-typical) | 0.01 Ω, 2000 F → τ = 20 s | — |
| EKF process noise `Q` | manually tuned diagonal covariance | `diag([5e-3, 1e-8])` | tuned for stable convergence on healthy data |
| EKF measurement noise `R` | manually tuned scalar | `8e-4` (V²) | tuned for stable convergence on healthy data |
| Initial state covariance `P0` | manually set | `diag([9.0, 1e-4])` | — |
| Residual threshold (`resid_max`) | 1.5 × max over healthy instances | ≈ 2.48 V | `normal_000`, `normal_001` |
| Temperature-rate threshold (`max dT/dt`) | 1.5 × max over healthy instances | ≈ 0.0385 °C/s | `normal_000`, `normal_001` |
| ICA peak-shift threshold | fixed engineering margin | 0.05 V | set relative to healthy peak location |
| Bus voltage z-score threshold | fixed engineering margin above observed healthy z-scores | −10.0 | `bus/normal_000`, `bus/normal_001` |
| Bus current z-score threshold | fixed engineering margin above observed healthy z-scores | 3.0 | `bus/normal_000`, `bus/normal_001` |

**No loss function, optimizer, epochs, or batch size** apply here — there is no neural network. The EKF's
internal "loss" is implicitly the weighted innovation `y² / S` it minimizes recursively at every timestep
(standard Kalman filter optimality under the assumed noise model), and the only offline optimization used
anywhere is a Savitzky–Golay smoothing pass (a fixed-window polynomial fit, not an iterative training loop).

**Caveat:** every threshold above is calibrated from only **2 healthy instances** — appropriate only as a
placeholder for this preview dataset. In production, calibrate as `mean + kσ` (e.g., k=3) over a much larger
healthy-fleet history.

